# What NOT to upload when deploying with the Vercel CLI.
#
# The CLI uploads this directory, so without this file the deploy would carry
# 113 MB of raw Kaggle input and the local .env files. Note that
# data_preprocessing/data_ready/ is deliberately NOT ignored: agent/catalog.py
# reads those CSVs at runtime and rag/store.py loads chunk_index.npz from there.

# Credentials. .env.example is a placeholder file and not needed at runtime.
.env
.env.*

# Raw Kaggle downloads: 113 MB, inputs to the preparation script only. Nothing
# at runtime touches them, and data_ready/ is generated from them offline.
data_preprocessing/data_full/

# Course PDFs and the pitch deck: 15 MB, not served by any route.
docs/

# Build-time accelerator: text -> vector, so re-running ingest never pays
# twice for an unchanged passage. rag/embed.py is its only reader and only
# during ingestion; nothing at runtime opens it. It is gitignored, but the CLI
# uploads the working directory rather than the git tree, so without this line
# it shipped 19.9 MB to production on every deploy -- nearly half the 50 MB
# data budget, spent on a file no request can reach.
data_preprocessing/data_ready/embedding_cache.npz

# Local-only
.git
.venv
venv
__pycache__
*.pyc
*.log
